CAT = "s6Disclosure"; SEG = "DIS"
Q = [
('A fund\'s statement of additional information must be provided:',
 'Free on request', ['With every confirmation', 'Only to institutions', 'For a fee by mail'],
 'The SAI holds more detail than the prospectus and is not required to be delivered, but the fund must send it free to anyone who asks.'),
('Investing a lump sum just before a sharp market drop is an example of:',
 'Timing risk', ['Issuer credit risk', 'Bond call risk', 'Currency risk'],
 'Timing risk is the risk of buying or selling at a bad moment. Spreading purchases over time is one way investors reduce it.'),
('Interest dividends from a national municipal bond fund are generally:',
 'Free of federal income tax', ['Taxed as qualified dividends', 'Taxed as capital gains', 'Taxed in every state'],
 'Tax-exempt interest keeps its federal exemption when a fund passes it through, though states may tax income from other states\' bonds.'),
('A rep moves a customer who trades twice a year into a wrap fee account. The main concern is that the customer:',
 'May pay more than in commissions', ['Will trade too often', 'Loses SIPC protection', 'Can no longer buy funds'],
 'For a buy-and-hold customer, a yearly asset-based fee can cost more than paying commissions on a few trades, so the account type itself must suit the customer under Reg BI.'),
('The federal gift and estate taxes are unified, meaning:',
 'One exemption covers both', ['Gifts are never taxable', 'Estates pay it first', 'Only estates are taxed'],
 'Taxable gifts during life use up the same lifetime exemption that would otherwise shelter the estate at death.'),
('Gifts within the annual exclusion:',
 'Do not reduce the exemption', ['Are taxed to the recipient', 'Must be made in cash', 'Count double against estates'],
 'Gifts up to the annual exclusion per recipient need no use of the lifetime exemption. Only gifts above it reduce the unified exemption.'),
('Under Rule 2165, an initial temporary hold on a senior\'s disbursement must end within:',
 '15 business days', ['5 business days', '30 calendar days', '60 calendar days'],
 'A Rule 2165 hold expires no later than 15 business days after it was placed unless extended under the rule or by a regulator or court.'),
('After placing a Rule 2165 hold, a firm generally notifies the trusted contact person within:',
 'Two business days', ['Twenty-four hours', 'Ten business days', 'Thirty days'],
 'Notice goes to authorized parties and the trusted contact within two business days, unless the firm believes that person is involved in the exploitation.'),
('A customer asks the firm to send copies of her confirmations to her accountant. The firm:',
 'May do so at her request', ['Must refuse under Reg S-P', 'Needs FINRA approval first', 'Must then stop sending hers'],
 'A customer may direct duplicate confirmations and statements to a third party such as an accountant. Regulation S-P permits sharing at the customer\'s direction, and she still gets her own copies.'),
('An investor\'s fund shares have risen $2,000 in value but have not been sold. That gain is:',
 'Unrealized', ['Realized', 'Taxable this year', 'A loss carryover'],
 'A gain is realized only when shares are sold. Until then it is unrealized and is not taxed, though the fund\'s own distributions may be.'),
('After a customer\'s change of address, the firm must notify the customer at the old and new addresses within:',
 '30 days', ['5 days', '10 days', '90 days'],
 'SEC Rule 17a-3 requires notice of an address change to be sent to both the old and new address within 30 days, to catch unauthorized changes.'),
('A rep moves to a new firm, which writes to the rep\'s former customer about moving assets. The letter must include:',
 'FINRA\'s education notice', ['The rep\'s new payout', 'Old firm\'s complaint file', 'A transfer fee waiver'],
 'Rule 2273 requires the recruiting firm to give former customers FINRA\'s educational communication on transferring assets, with the first written contact, for three months after the rep joins.'),
('Under Rule 11870, after validating an account transfer, the carrying firm must complete it within:',
 'Three business days', ['Fifteen business days', 'Five business days', 'Ten business days'],
 'Rule 11870 gives the carrying firm one business day to validate or take exception and three business days after validation to complete the transfer.'),
('During an account transfer, a proprietary fund cannot be moved. The carrying firm must:',
 'Ask the customer what to do', ['Sell it without telling the customer', 'Keep it without telling anyone', 'Send it to the new rep'],
 'Rule 11870 requires a list of nontransferable assets and a request for instructions: liquidate, keep with the carrying firm, or transfer as the rule allows.'),
('A fund\'s yearly turnover ratio of 150% generally suggests:',
 'Higher trading costs', ['Lower trading costs', 'A passive index strategy', 'Fewer tax distributions'],
 'High turnover means the portfolio is replaced often, raising commissions and spreads and often producing more taxable gains.'),
('A fund\'s expense ratio includes:',
 'Management and 12b-1 fees', ['Front-end sales loads', 'Deferred sales charges', 'Separate brokerage account fees'],
 'The expense ratio shows yearly operating costs as a share of assets, including management and 12b-1 fees. Sales loads are charged on purchases or redemptions instead.'),
]
